  "updated_at": "2025-10-04T22:10:00Z",
  "global_notes": [
    "Halide reactivity: I > Br >> Cl; unactivated ArCl typically require bulky, electron-rich monophosphines (XPhos, Ligand 95) and higher temperature.",
    "Water (10–30%) often accelerates boronate activation, but minimize water for boron partners prone to protodeboronation (e.g., 2-pyridyl, 2-furyl, 2-thienyl).",
    "Bases most common in the dataset themes: K2CO3/K3PO4/Cs2CO3; KOAc is preferred for Miyaura borylation; avoid very strong alkoxides unless specifically required (e.g., dan activation with KOtBu).",
    "For heteroaryl systems that coordinate strongly (pyridines, azines), rapid-activation precatalysts and slow-release boron (MIDA/BF3K) are helpful.",
    "If protodeboronation or hydrolysis dominates, lower temperature, reduce water, consider masked boron or switch to stabilized boronates."
  ]
}